WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.240
Netflix's "The Silent Sea" ended on one heck of a&nbsp;
cliffhanger. What's going to happen to Luna? Will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.600
the truth of the Belhae station come to light?&nbsp;
This is the end of "The Silent Sea" explained.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.640
So what really happens in the final moments&nbsp;
of the first season? The final episode of "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.120
Silent Sea" ends with a rescue ship arriving&nbsp;
with the intent of heading back to Earth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.520
But not much else is known for certain,&nbsp;
including the health of Song, Hong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:30.160
and Luna. Everyone else from the mission dies&nbsp;
in one way or another, with the two doctors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.640
and the child being the only survivors.&nbsp;
Even Han, who seems so close to surviving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.960
sacrifices himself in the final moments&nbsp;
so that the others can escape with Luna.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.840
As for the lunar water, they have some samples,&nbsp;
but there's no way anyone else can get more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.360
as Balhae Station is completely&nbsp;
destroyed by the water itself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.000
This gets rid of one problem for Song, as&nbsp;
it means that RX and other organizations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.200
won't try to retrieve more samples,&nbsp;
but they still don't even know how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.280
the water was found in the first place.&nbsp;
But with Luna and a few samples, Song,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.160
Hong, and other like-minded researchers could&nbsp;
potentially discover the answers for themselves.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.920
For people like Captain&nbsp;
Han, Director Choi, and Ryu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.600
their desperation to find an answer&nbsp;
is simply to improve their own status.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:16.000
They need lunar water to be the thing that&nbsp;
saves everyone, just as Song's sister did.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.400
In the case of Song and Hong, the two doctors&nbsp;
who represent the other end of the spectrum,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.800
they believe in the mission to a point. But&nbsp;
they also know that there's no miracle cure to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:29.600
the world water crisis, and from the beginning,&nbsp;
they are clear about their value of human life.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.640
Song and Hong know to ask whether it is really&nbsp;
worth it, especially after witnessing firsthand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:39.360
how brutal and deadly lunar water really is.&nbsp;
While Song would love for the water to be the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.480
ultimate cure, she isn't willing to sacrifice the&nbsp;
lives of those around her just for some dream.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.480
Throughout Season 1, Captain Han shares the same&nbsp;
pragmatic, logical understanding as Song, but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:54.880
has his daughter to fight for, so he's willing&nbsp;
to do almost anything to complete the mission.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.280
But then enters Luna, a superpowered little&nbsp;
girl who is desperate to keep the lunar water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.480
to herself. Song sees through the violence and&nbsp;
realizes that it's not a monster attacking them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:08.640
but a girl who can survive the water. Through&nbsp;
further investigation, it's discovered that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.600
Balhae crew were experimenting with the water&nbsp;
on numbered clones known as "Luna." Each time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.720
the girls died, until number 73, which is&nbsp;
the Luna the crew meets upon their arrival.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.200
Even after discovering all of this, Han still&nbsp;
has one goal, and that's finding the samples and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.920
bringing them back to Earth, even if that means&nbsp;
killing Luna. But once they meet face to face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.320
Luna is the final straw for Han, bringing him&nbsp;
to his senses about what's really important.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:36.080
She reminds him of his daughter, who looks&nbsp;
to be around the same age and desperately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.240
needs water to survive. The entire reason&nbsp;
he goes on the mission is for his daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.880
but Luna reminds him that there are other children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:47.520
and other people that matter just as much. While&nbsp;
the water sample is still a major priority,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.440
Luna's survival, and the hope that she&nbsp;
can live a real life, is the true mission.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.160
There are plenty of unanswered questions at&nbsp;
the end of "The Silent Sea" Season 1. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.360
two biggest mysteries are Luna and lunar water,&nbsp;
as there's still not a lot known about either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.360
In the penultimate episode, Ryu insinuates&nbsp;
to Han that there's much more about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.040
original mission, and the lunar water&nbsp;
itself, that they don't know, saying,

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:19.280
"You don't know anything. Nothing about&nbsp;
what happened and what the lunar water…"

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:23.040
He's right. For example, if they&nbsp;
were finding success with Luna 73,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.840
what really led Choi to shut down the study?

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.560
Of course, there's also everything about Luna&nbsp;
that we don't know. While she can clearly survive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.280
the lunar water, it doesn't just sustain her,&nbsp;
but it also gives her advanced healing, speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.920
strength, eyesight, and probably a lot more.&nbsp;
Oh, and she can also survive in the moon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.560
atmosphere. So how does all this happen?&nbsp;
We see the experiments that led to Luna 73,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:48.000
but not much else about her background.&nbsp;
As for her connection to the water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.800
Luna's bite allows Song to survive the&nbsp;
water's infection, but what else might it do?

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.400
Although "The Silent Sea" Season 1 ends with&nbsp;
only a few of the original crew left standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.320
and a rescue ship arriving, the&nbsp;
events after that are unclear.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:05.840
Early on in Episode 8, Song declares&nbsp;
her plan for Luna and herself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.320
stating that she will escort them both to the&nbsp;
International Institute of Space Biology. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.800
show provides a short look at the IISB,&nbsp;
though nothing else about it is revealed.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.360
As Song states that they can't bring the sample&nbsp;
or Luna back to Earth, we can assume that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:24.480
enacts a plan to get to the IISB, which&nbsp;
would likely be explored in Season 2. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:29.040
though it portrays itself as neutral territory,&nbsp;
there will probably be trouble there as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:33.280
Also, there's no way Choi or RX are&nbsp;
letting this resource go without a fight.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.360
There's also the question of whether or not&nbsp;
to reveal the truth about Balhae Station,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:42.400
which is brought up earlier in the final episode.&nbsp;
Both Hong and Song want to expose the truth of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:46.960
what happened on the station, but this would&nbsp;
likely have huge ramifications for everyone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.760
If a second season does come to Netflix, we can&nbsp;
expect this plot thread to be further explored.

